<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christine of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–<a href="/years/1663">1663</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Christine Marie of France</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, daughter of Henry IV and Marie de' Medici, married Victor Amadeus I of Savoy in 1619. After his death in 1637 she ruled as regent for her young sons and faced a civil war in 1639–1642 against her brothers-in-law Cardinal Maurice and Prince Thomas, who were backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Known as the Madama Reale, she kept Savoy allied with France and influenced government until her death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christine-of-france.jpg" alt="Christine of France" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: French School / Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:French_School_-_Christine_of_France,_Duchess_of_Savoy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
